<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 283 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 283 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 283 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>The Bank allotted 173 million outright in bills maturing on or before March 19 and 110 million in repos to March 18 and 19.</p>
<p>It has now provided liquidity of 653 million stg in total on Wednesday. The shortage is forecast at 950 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
